WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:03.571 --> 00:00:05.540
<i>Previously on</i> Marshals...

2
00:00:05.607 --> 00:00:06.741
Hey! Hey!

3
00:00:06.808 --> 00:00:08.008
Hey! Hey!

4
00:00:08.075 --> 00:00:09.544
-Stallion's moving on.
-He's Mom's.

5
00:00:09.611 --> 00:00:11.111
<i>You can't just erase</i>
<i>every memory of her.</i>

6
00:00:11.178 --> 00:00:13.515
I didn't cry
at my dad's funeral.

7
00:00:13.581 --> 00:00:16.083
I was too overwhelmed
by the loss to actually grieve.

8
00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:19.219
<i>It was nice of</i>
<i>your husband and kid to drop by.</i>

9
00:00:19.286 --> 00:00:21.756
You know. building walls
shuts out the people

10
00:00:21.823 --> 00:00:23.123
<i>that you care about.</i>

11
00:00:24.526 --> 00:00:26.026
<i>You saved my life.</i>

12
00:00:26.093 --> 00:00:27.461
Let me lend you some hands.

13
00:00:27.529 --> 00:00:28.830
Well. good day for you.
You kept your badge

14
00:00:28.897 --> 00:00:29.998
and you made a new friend.

15
00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:31.465
Saddle up. cowboy.

16
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:39.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

17
00:01:05.332 --> 00:01:08.168
What part of evolve or die
do you not understand?

18
00:01:37.264 --> 00:01:40.100
Here to check
on your dad's hands.

19
00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.003
they're moving the herd.

20
00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:43.403
I was out exploring.

21
00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.573
Had a vague memory
of you promising

22
00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.275
to give this newbie
an insider's tour.

23
00:01:49.343 --> 00:01:51.311
Pretty sure I said "maybe."

24
00:01:51.378 --> 00:01:52.412
So you'd rather wrestle
that horse than show me

25
00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:53.848
what's so great about Montana?

26
00:01:55.984 --> 00:01:57.919
Try and keep up.

27
00:02:10.832 --> 00:02:13.166
Reminds me of the Pyrenees.

28
00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:15.202
Alps. too.

29
00:02:16.838 --> 00:02:18.906
Yeah?
You done a lot of traveling?

30
00:02:18.973 --> 00:02:20.742
Yeah. Growing up.

31
00:02:20.808 --> 00:02:23.310
we'd take family trips
every summer and Christmas.

32
00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.445
You?

33
00:02:25.513 --> 00:02:27.782
I had to join the Navy
to see the world.

34
00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:32.654
And just think.

35
00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:34.656
this was left by a glacier
10.000 years ago.

36
00:02:34.722 --> 00:02:37.025
It's also the spot where I took
my brother Jamie's clothes

37
00:02:37.091 --> 00:02:39.661
while he was skinny-dipping.
He had to ride home bare-assed.

38
00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:43.831
Must've been a dream

39
00:02:43.898 --> 00:02:46.466
growing up with
the world's greatest backyard.

40
00:02:48.069 --> 00:02:49.937
Handle that horse pretty well.

41
00:02:50.738 --> 00:02:52.674
Believe it or not.
there are stables in the city.

42
00:03:01.516 --> 00:03:02.950
You said
you'd been experiencing

43
00:03:03.017 --> 00:03:04.351
some neck and shoulder pain?

44
00:03:04.418 --> 00:03:05.653
Some tingling in the hand?

45
00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.255
How long have you had
these symptoms?

46
00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:11.592
Since the first door
I breached. I just...

47
00:03:11.659 --> 00:03:13.493
I've learned to live with them.

48
00:03:14.696 --> 00:03:16.731
How many deployments
did you have?

49
00:03:17.799 --> 00:03:20.568
More than I can remember.
literally.

50
00:03:22.036 --> 00:03:26.206
Well. we'll run some tests.
try to find you some answers.

51
00:03:28.308 --> 00:03:30.011
Okay.

52
00:03:39.153 --> 00:03:40.855
See you later.

53
00:03:41.956 --> 00:03:44.025
Cal?

54
00:03:44.092 --> 00:03:45.626
What are you doing here?

55
00:03:45.693 --> 00:03:47.294
Belle hasn't mentioned
your team is

56
00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.428
running down fugitive doctors.

57
00:03:48.495 --> 00:03:49.764
Hey. Jared.

58
00:03:49.831 --> 00:03:52.499
Uh. nah. I was just. um.
getting a checkup.

59
00:03:53.935 --> 00:03:57.437
Yeah. I was at a work lunch.
Should get back to the office.

60
00:03:57.505 --> 00:03:59.941
Right. It's good seeing you.

61
00:04:00.007 --> 00:04:01.109
Yeah.

62
00:04:16.691 --> 00:04:18.092
Your dad make you
uproot your life

63
00:04:18.159 --> 00:04:19.326
to move all the way out here?

64
00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:22.429
I'm a grown woman.

65
00:04:22.496 --> 00:04:24.799
Can't make me do anything.

66
00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.267
I'm here because I love him.

67
00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:30.104
and because he made me partner
in his new cattle venture.

68
00:04:31.471 --> 00:04:32.372
Dad. what're you doing here?

69
00:04:34.575 --> 00:04:37.444
Kayce broke my leg.

70
00:04:37.512 --> 00:04:39.479
Had to make sure
you were safe. pumpkin.

71
00:04:39.547 --> 00:04:41.949
I believe

72
00:04:42.016 --> 00:04:44.351
you brought me a hat.
last time I saw you.

73
00:04:45.553 --> 00:04:48.990
Allow me to return the favor.

74
00:04:49.056 --> 00:04:52.492
It's good to see you up
on your feet so soon. sir.

75
00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.962
No days off on the ranch. right?

76
00:04:55.029 --> 00:04:58.498
And I healed enough
I managed to bag an elk.

77
00:04:58.566 --> 00:05:02.469
I figured I'd make dinner.
pay down my debt to you.

78
00:05:03.905 --> 00:05:06.373
Well. I know better than to
refuse an offer from a Weaver.

79
00:05:08.009 --> 00:05:10.144
Great.

80
00:05:13.748 --> 00:05:16.383
Here... Here you go. Miles.

81
00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.186
Uh. the tea was a little tart.

82
00:05:18.252 --> 00:05:21.122
so I-I spiked it
with a sugar cube.

83
00:05:21.189 --> 00:05:23.124
Appreciate it.

84
00:05:28.629 --> 00:05:30.430
Feel bad rolling you
on Mom's night out.

85
00:05:30.497 --> 00:05:32.633
Eh...

86
00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:36.037
Jared and Braxton left
for a father-son camping trip.

87
00:05:36.103 --> 00:05:39.207
so I got all night
to take your money.

88
00:05:39.273 --> 00:05:41.008
Mm. Who you betting on?

89
00:05:41.075 --> 00:05:43.578
After seeing Belle
as a biker chick.

90
00:05:43.644 --> 00:05:45.813
I got no doubt
she's got some hustler in her.

91
00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:47.480
Mm.

92
00:05:47.548 --> 00:05:49.183
My money's on Miles.

93
00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:52.820
Broken Rock's luck is turning.
thanks to its guardian angel.

94
00:05:52.887 --> 00:05:56.557
Sabrina. these are my teammates.
Belle and Andrea.

95
00:05:56.624 --> 00:05:57.825
They helped find
the missing girls.

96
00:05:57.892 --> 00:06:00.595
Well. look at you.
sharing credit.

97
00:06:00.661 --> 00:06:01.762
You know.
for a former college athlete.

98
00:06:01.829 --> 00:06:03.064
you have a pretty small ego.

99
00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.099
"College athlete" is a stretch.

100
00:06:05.166 --> 00:06:08.769
All state tight end
and linebacker. full ride

101
00:06:08.836 --> 00:06:10.705
- to a D1 program.
- Damn. Miles.

102
00:06:10.771 --> 00:06:13.207
I knew you played. but
I didn't know you were a player.

103
00:06:13.274 --> 00:06:15.710
I wasn't. Dropped the ball.

104
00:06:15.776 --> 00:06:18.045
Miles and the coach didn't
see eye to eye.

105
00:06:18.112 --> 00:06:19.814
Dust Cloud being Dust Cloud.

106
00:06:19.881 --> 00:06:21.148
I've mellowed.

107
00:06:21.215 --> 00:06:22.683
Hopefully not too much.

108
00:06:24.919 --> 00:06:27.054
Nice meeting you.

109
00:06:27.121 --> 00:06:30.224
Miles's friends.
Give me a call sometime. Miles.

110
00:06:35.897 --> 00:06:39.233
All right. This does bring up
a very important question.

111
00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:41.102
Are you dating anyone?

112
00:06:41.168 --> 00:06:43.070
No.

113
00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:45.940
You like someone.

114
00:06:46.007 --> 00:06:47.440
It's complicated.

115
00:06:47.508 --> 00:06:50.544
She's not from where I'm from.

116
00:06:50.611 --> 00:06:53.180
-So?
-So. like my football career.

117
00:06:53.247 --> 00:06:54.882
it's probably not meant to be.

118
00:07:01.122 --> 00:07:02.790
I know. it was delicious.

119
00:07:02.857 --> 00:07:04.424
I think I want to come back
next week.

120
00:07:04.491 --> 00:07:07.094
- Yeah. We will.
- Yeah. good. Good. good. good.

121
00:07:10.064 --> 00:07:11.399
I forgot the leftovers.

122
00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:12.800
Blake...

123
00:07:12.867 --> 00:07:14.235
All right. I'm going back.

124
00:07:14.302 --> 00:07:16.637
Shoot. I left my glasses inside.
Just be a minute.

125
00:07:16.704 --> 00:07:18.005
I'll keep it running.
Your Honor.

126
00:08:02.817 --> 00:08:06.587
Good job. sir.
Most people overcook elk.

127
00:08:06.654 --> 00:08:08.723
Mm. Dad's the chef
in the family.

128
00:08:08.789 --> 00:08:11.659
I got an unwanted promotion
to house cook.

129
00:08:11.726 --> 00:08:13.260
I can't compete with you.

130
00:08:14.128 --> 00:08:15.396
How I feel
about you and your family

131
00:08:15.463 --> 00:08:16.664
when it comes to ranching.

132
00:08:16.731 --> 00:08:18.699
Hmm. Why he pays
a team of brainiacs

133
00:08:18.766 --> 00:08:19.834
with ag degrees to help.

134
00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:21.635
Doing more than helping.

135
00:08:21.702 --> 00:08:23.437
They've pointed me
toward some technologies

136
00:08:23.504 --> 00:08:25.806
to up my chances for success.

137
00:08:25.873 --> 00:08:28.709
Well. I was raised to believe
the old ways are the right ways.

138
00:08:28.776 --> 00:08:31.512
From what I hear.
the old ways included

139
00:08:31.579 --> 00:08:34.015
the Yellowstone never turning
a profit.

140
00:08:34.081 --> 00:08:37.518
Well. the way of life
is the true reward

141
00:08:37.585 --> 00:08:39.153
when it comes to ranching. sir.

142
00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:41.622
Not with my investors.

143
00:08:41.689 --> 00:08:44.158
If-if I can put my thumb
on the scale.

144
00:08:44.225 --> 00:08:45.393
why wouldn't I?

145
00:08:45.459 --> 00:08:47.762
DNA marker testing
helped me pick

146
00:08:47.828 --> 00:08:49.096
the most productive cattle
to start with.

147
00:08:49.163 --> 00:08:51.232
and now.
I'm tracking them using RFID

148
00:08:51.298 --> 00:08:52.933
to keep my labor costs down.

149
00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.703
Sounds like a hefty
up-front cost.

150
00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:58.507
That's why I spread the risk.

151
00:08:58.572 --> 00:09:01.375
Offer each head
as an individual asset

152
00:09:01.442 --> 00:09:03.210
folks can invest in.

153
00:09:03.277 --> 00:09:06.547
That working capital
increases my valuation.

154
00:09:08.315 --> 00:09:10.217
You and my sister'd get along.

155
00:09:10.284 --> 00:09:13.554
I'm in it
for the long haul. Kayce.

156
00:09:13.621 --> 00:09:15.056
More land. more cattle.

157
00:09:15.122 --> 00:09:17.324
That's how I attract
more investors.

158
00:09:18.726 --> 00:09:20.961
I would love

159
00:09:21.028 --> 00:09:23.964
to make East Camp
part of my operation.

160
00:09:30.004 --> 00:09:31.906
You want to buy my ranch?

161
00:09:37.044 --> 00:09:39.947
Geez. Dad. give him dessert
before asking him into bed.

162
00:09:40.014 --> 00:09:43.050
I'm direct when I see
something I want.

163
00:09:44.785 --> 00:09:47.855
Hmm. Thank you for dinner.

164
00:09:49.657 --> 00:09:51.725
Uh. let us help clean up.

165
00:09:51.792 --> 00:09:55.262
No. dishes are one thing
I can handle in the kitchen.

166
00:09:55.329 --> 00:09:59.333
I meant no. uh. no offense.

167
00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:02.103
We can both come out winners.

168
00:10:02.169 --> 00:10:04.105
Think it over.

169
00:10:17.985 --> 00:10:19.620
Was that some sort of plan

170
00:10:19.687 --> 00:10:22.156
to soften me up
so your dad could make an offer

171
00:10:22.223 --> 00:10:23.457
on East Camp?

172
00:10:23.525 --> 00:10:25.793
I was as blindsided as you.

173
00:10:26.794 --> 00:10:30.064
It's why my family never talks
business at the dinner table.

174
00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:38.239
I'm sorry.

175
00:10:41.408 --> 00:10:43.811
We were having fun
until he ruined it.

176
00:10:43.878 --> 00:10:46.247
Weren't we?

177
00:10:47.414 --> 00:10:48.617
Yeah.

178
00:10:48.682 --> 00:10:51.051
Thank you for a lovely day.

179
00:10:58.759 --> 00:11:01.695
Good night.

180
00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:15.676
Hey. Got something
you want to tell me?

181
00:11:15.743 --> 00:11:16.944
About what?

182
00:11:17.011 --> 00:11:19.514
Ghosting us at the bar
last night.

183
00:11:19.581 --> 00:11:22.316
Ah. Yeah.
Day got away from me. My bad.

184
00:11:22.383 --> 00:11:23.784
Uh-huh.

185
00:11:23.851 --> 00:11:24.818
Hey. Gifford called.

186
00:11:24.885 --> 00:11:26.387
We've got something.

187
00:11:26.453 --> 00:11:28.557
Federal Judge Pauline Ayers
and her husband Blake

188
00:11:28.623 --> 00:11:30.925
- survived a car bomb attack.
- Yeah. I saw that.

189
00:11:30.991 --> 00:11:32.661
The valet wasn't so lucky.

190
00:11:32.726 --> 00:11:34.361
You got any leads on a suspect?

191
00:11:34.428 --> 00:11:38.365
A federal judge likely
has a long list of enemies.

192
00:11:38.432 --> 00:11:41.268
Clint Gallo.
Threatened revenge ten years ago

193
00:11:41.335 --> 00:11:42.903
when Ayers sentenced him
to prison

194
00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.972
for the bombing
of a women's health center.

195
00:11:45.039 --> 00:11:46.774
Paroled last month.
Missed a check-in

196
00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:47.908
with his P.O. last week.

197
00:11:47.975 --> 00:11:49.644
Well. that makes him a fugitive.

198
00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:52.079
Yeah. The FBI's got the lead on
the bombing. but Gallo's ours.

199
00:11:52.146 --> 00:11:54.982
Judicial protection falls under
the Marshals' purview.

200
00:11:55.049 --> 00:11:56.483
Are we watching over Ayers?

201
00:11:56.551 --> 00:11:59.119
And her family. until
her attacker's in custody.

202
00:11:59.186 --> 00:12:01.755
Cowboy and I can hunt down
the ex-con while the rest of you

203
00:12:01.822 --> 00:12:03.390
shack up with the happy family?

204
00:12:07.596 --> 00:12:11.365
Yeah. Last thing we need
is an open season on judges.

205
00:12:18.239 --> 00:12:19.740
I know it feels like

206
00:12:19.807 --> 00:12:21.308
we're punishing
the victims here. but...

207
00:12:21.375 --> 00:12:23.077
but given the bomber
knew your pattern of life.

208
00:12:23.143 --> 00:12:24.478
we're-we're gonna
have to restrict

209
00:12:24.546 --> 00:12:25.946
your family's movements.

210
00:12:26.013 --> 00:12:28.449
Your marshal doing
the security sweep is gonna

211
00:12:28.516 --> 00:12:29.684
spook our neighbors.

212
00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:32.753
Uh. you...
do you have any leads?

213
00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:34.989
We're eyeing a violent convict

214
00:12:35.055 --> 00:12:36.757
you sent away years ago.

215
00:12:36.824 --> 00:12:40.595
Oh. Well. that
really narrows it down.

216
00:12:40.662 --> 00:12:42.396
We're gonna do our best to stay
out of your hair. Your Honor.

217
00:12:42.463 --> 00:12:45.332
Oh. knock that
"Your Honor" crap off.

218
00:12:45.399 --> 00:12:46.867
Hey.

219
00:12:46.934 --> 00:12:49.937
Oh. Magic City
Nonprofit of the Year

220
00:12:50.004 --> 00:12:53.173
2023. Chiron's Care.

221
00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:54.942
I'm the. uh.
executive director.

222
00:12:55.009 --> 00:12:56.343
We get medical equipment

223
00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:58.212
to underserved communities
around the world.

224
00:12:58.279 --> 00:13:00.314
He's the softie.
I'm the hard-ass.

225
00:13:01.415 --> 00:13:03.652
Well. if you need
dental supplies.

226
00:13:03.718 --> 00:13:04.918
I can connect you to my husband.

227
00:13:04.985 --> 00:13:06.954
He's a do-gooder. too.

228
00:13:07.021 --> 00:13:09.658
Franny says Lulu
wants the ticket

229
00:13:09.724 --> 00:13:11.660
to MountainLoaf if I can't go.

230
00:13:11.726 --> 00:13:13.794
The. uh. music festival
next month?

231
00:13:13.861 --> 00:13:15.262
Yeah.

232
00:13:15.329 --> 00:13:17.798
Well. honey. if you're
still under protection

233
00:13:17.865 --> 00:13:20.535
by then.
we have failed at our job.

234
00:13:20.602 --> 00:13:23.738
Even if you succeed.
Blake and I

235
00:13:23.804 --> 00:13:25.774
haven't said that Fallon can go.

236
00:13:29.544 --> 00:13:30.578
My mistake.

237
00:13:34.415 --> 00:13:37.051
This is where
Gallo's girlfriend lives?

238
00:13:37.117 --> 00:13:39.353
Guess she's got a kink
for convicts.

239
00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.388
Okay. so. Gallo took a shot
at the judge

240
00:13:41.455 --> 00:13:42.890
after serving ten years?

241
00:13:42.956 --> 00:13:44.491
Values vengeance over freedom.

242
00:13:44.559 --> 00:13:46.160
Seems like a trade you'd make.

243
00:13:46.226 --> 00:13:47.595
Hey.

244
00:13:47.662 --> 00:13:50.064
Clint Gallo?

245
00:13:54.068 --> 00:13:55.469
U.S. Marshals!

246
00:14:04.478 --> 00:14:06.614
Tossed him
like an angry bronc.

247
00:14:06.681 --> 00:14:08.683
You're sounding more Montanan
every day.

248
00:14:12.554 --> 00:14:15.289
You know. much of my work
is confidential.

249
00:14:15.356 --> 00:14:17.124
The Fusion Center
won't break privilege.

250
00:14:17.191 --> 00:14:20.060
they'll just analyze the threats
you've gotten.

251
00:14:20.127 --> 00:14:23.531
Hope they're working in shifts.

252
00:14:23.598 --> 00:14:25.533
Your husband give you
a hard time

253
00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:27.368
for going after the worst of us?

254
00:14:28.202 --> 00:14:31.071
It's a constant negotiation.

255
00:14:31.138 --> 00:14:34.208
but we always find
common ground.

256
00:14:35.376 --> 00:14:37.612
Unfortunately for me.
judges don't negotiate.

257
00:14:41.516 --> 00:14:43.250
Your Honor-- Ma'am?

258
00:14:43.317 --> 00:14:45.687
We're gonna need you to stay
where we can keep eyes on.

259
00:14:45.754 --> 00:14:47.221
I need to use the bathroom.

260
00:14:47.287 --> 00:14:49.456
Use your daughter's.
There's no windows.

261
00:14:49.524 --> 00:14:51.392
Stay out of there.
I'm tie-dyeing a dress

262
00:14:51.458 --> 00:14:52.459
for MountainLoaf.

263
00:14:52.527 --> 00:14:54.294
Don't get
ahead of yourself.

264
00:14:54.361 --> 00:14:55.963
We should let her go.
have some normal teenage fun

265
00:14:56.029 --> 00:14:57.732
after all this.

266
00:14:57.799 --> 00:14:59.166
Hey. you heard Mom.

267
00:14:59.233 --> 00:15:01.603
No chance Maximum Pauline
shows me any leniency.

268
00:15:01.669 --> 00:15:04.873
Great. I'm the bad guy. Again.

269
00:15:09.577 --> 00:15:11.780
You think we should warn them
the last thing they want

270
00:15:11.846 --> 00:15:13.848
is their daughter
picking sides between them?

271
00:15:13.914 --> 00:15:17.217
She's got enough on her plate
with someone trying to kill her.

272
00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:21.388
But if you know something
that affects somebody's family.

273
00:15:21.455 --> 00:15:24.124
I mean.
you should say something. right?

274
00:15:25.025 --> 00:15:28.696
Family drama should stay
in the family.

275
00:15:33.467 --> 00:15:35.436
<i>Threatened the judge last decade</i>

276
00:15:35.503 --> 00:15:37.404
<i>and enacted your vengeance</i>
<i>last night.</i>

277
00:15:37.471 --> 00:15:39.473
You sure can hold a grudge.
I'll give you that.

278
00:15:39.541 --> 00:15:43.076
-Ayers is dead?
-Nope. but a valet is.

279
00:15:43.143 --> 00:15:47.549
I was at Teresa's all yesterday.
She'll vouch for me.

280
00:15:47.615 --> 00:15:50.317
Doesn't matter.
When the bomb went off

281
00:15:50.384 --> 00:15:53.387
and when it was planted
are two different timelines.

282
00:15:53.454 --> 00:15:56.423
I got better things to do
than settle some old score.

283
00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:59.326
Way she dropped the hammer.
cops are getting

284
00:15:59.393 --> 00:16:01.529
pretty lazy if they think
I'm the only one

285
00:16:01.596 --> 00:16:02.797
dreamt of murdering her.

286
00:16:08.402 --> 00:16:11.271
I'm trapped in my home.
like Elsa.

287
00:16:11.338 --> 00:16:13.974
No one wants
to hear this. honey.

288
00:16:14.041 --> 00:16:16.744
Maybe this is a blessing
in disguise.

289
00:16:16.811 --> 00:16:21.448
A chance to put family first.
the way you talk about. Hmm?

290
00:16:24.017 --> 00:16:27.221
That guy sure seems thirsty
for his wife's attention.

291
00:16:27.287 --> 00:16:30.457
What's with your need to play
Dr. Phil with them?

292
00:16:30.525 --> 00:16:33.160
Nothing. We just both know
that putting all in at work

293
00:16:33.227 --> 00:16:35.095
can fracture relationships.

294
00:16:37.799 --> 00:16:39.466
Speak for yourself.

295
00:16:41.970 --> 00:16:43.303
Fallon. no!

296
00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:45.405
Get down. get down!

297
00:16:45.472 --> 00:16:48.242
Away from the window.

298
00:16:52.547 --> 00:16:54.114
It's okay. baby. You're fine.

299
00:16:54.181 --> 00:16:55.783
Someone's trying to kill you.
Nothing is fine.

300
00:16:57.017 --> 00:16:58.620
Blue. blue.

301
00:17:00.087 --> 00:17:02.690
So? Any trace of the shooter?

302
00:17:02.757 --> 00:17:03.892
Negative.

303
00:17:03.958 --> 00:17:05.660
Only place shots
could've come from

304
00:17:05.727 --> 00:17:07.160
is the parking garage
across the street.

305
00:17:07.227 --> 00:17:09.329
Didn't find any casings.

306
00:17:09.396 --> 00:17:11.231
Shooter cleared out too fast
to be on foot.

307
00:17:11.298 --> 00:17:12.667
We're getting security footage.

308
00:17:12.734 --> 00:17:15.803
Does Gallo's sheet have
any long guns work?

309
00:17:15.870 --> 00:17:17.605
Kayce and Andrea apprehended him

310
00:17:17.672 --> 00:17:19.641
well before
these shots were fired.

311
00:17:19.707 --> 00:17:21.208
Okay. well.
if he's not our shooter.

312
00:17:21.275 --> 00:17:22.877
then we can't still like him
for the bombing.

313
00:17:22.944 --> 00:17:24.979
Only thing certain is that
the assassin knows

314
00:17:25.045 --> 00:17:26.179
where the judge is. so...

315
00:17:26.246 --> 00:17:27.582
Listen up. y'all.

316
00:17:27.649 --> 00:17:30.050
Ayers family.
there's a change of venue. okay?

317
00:17:30.117 --> 00:17:32.020
You're coming to our house now.

318
00:17:32.085 --> 00:17:34.689
Local PD is coming in
to take over the crime scene.

319
00:17:34.756 --> 00:17:36.858
I can hold here
in case anything comes up.

320
00:17:36.925 --> 00:17:39.359
There must be some way
that you can keep me safe

321
00:17:39.426 --> 00:17:41.829
and not make my family
feel like prisoners.

322
00:17:46.333 --> 00:17:48.703
Hey. I know a place

323
00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:51.005
off-grid. okay.
that we can tuck these two away.

324
00:17:51.071 --> 00:17:53.440
Okay? But you're coming with us.

325
00:17:53.508 --> 00:17:54.341
Yeah.

326
00:17:54.408 --> 00:17:56.911
Okay. come on. y'all. Let's go.

327
00:17:56.978 --> 00:17:58.513
It's gonna be okay.

328
00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:01.281
Takes an assassination attempt
on a judge

329
00:18:01.348 --> 00:18:03.150
for an invite to your place.

330
00:18:03.216 --> 00:18:05.085
I think you're confusing
an order from Cal

331
00:18:05.152 --> 00:18:06.588
for a social gathering.

332
00:18:06.654 --> 00:18:08.790
Weaver Ranch?

333
00:18:08.856 --> 00:18:11.258
I see who your social
invitations are reserved for.

334
00:18:12.894 --> 00:18:14.261
Blue. blue.

335
00:18:14.328 --> 00:18:16.864
Blake. Fallon.
I want you to meet

336
00:18:16.931 --> 00:18:18.866
Deputy Marshals Dutton and Cruz.

337
00:18:18.933 --> 00:18:21.035
Apologies for the intrusion.

338
00:18:21.101 --> 00:18:22.402
Oh. don't apologize.

339
00:18:22.469 --> 00:18:24.038
I understand
how you must be feeling.

340
00:18:24.104 --> 00:18:25.773
I believe you do.

341
00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:27.441
What's that mean?

342
00:18:28.208 --> 00:18:31.646
It means we're in good hands
with Deputy Marshal Dutton.

343
00:18:31.713 --> 00:18:33.447
Good. Then he can find

344
00:18:33.514 --> 00:18:36.818
who's trying to kill Mom
and we can go home.

345
00:18:46.761 --> 00:18:49.530
If Gallo isn't our guy.
then any new theories on who is?

346
00:18:49.597 --> 00:18:52.000
Yeah.
FBI forensics have concluded

347
00:18:52.066 --> 00:18:53.835
that the bomb from the car
is more commonly seen

348
00:18:53.901 --> 00:18:56.403
in the African Sahel
than in domestic terrorism.

349
00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:58.773
Yeah. that type of bomb making

350
00:18:58.840 --> 00:19:00.608
and sniper skillset
feels military.

351
00:19:00.675 --> 00:19:02.476
Agree. That's why
we're cross-referencing

352
00:19:02.543 --> 00:19:05.647
the judge's sentencing records
with military jackets. but

353
00:19:05.713 --> 00:19:09.282
till we find that assassin.
y'all keep your heads down.

354
00:19:13.487 --> 00:19:15.657
Was it Tom or Dolly
who came over?

355
00:19:17.692 --> 00:19:20.695
Sounds like we'll be here
for a while. You'll tell me.

356
00:19:20.762 --> 00:19:23.564
I'm doing a security sweep.

357
00:19:23.631 --> 00:19:25.232
Okay.

358
00:19:25.298 --> 00:19:27.769
Security cams caught
a red van entering the garage

359
00:19:27.835 --> 00:19:30.370
15 minutes before the shooting
and exiting shortly after.

360
00:19:30.437 --> 00:19:32.239
No plates. but we're
sending you the footage.

361
00:19:33.141 --> 00:19:34.441
Take what we can get
at this point.

362
00:19:34.509 --> 00:19:35.810
And my team found these

363
00:19:35.877 --> 00:19:38.613
hidden in the wall
near the bullet hits.

364
00:19:44.085 --> 00:19:46.420
Looks like the judge's husband.

365
00:19:47.855 --> 00:19:50.558
Why's a nonprofit director
need an alias?

366
00:19:51.425 --> 00:19:53.427
I'll give you
some privacy. ma'am.

367
00:19:56.964 --> 00:19:59.734
Well. judge is settled in.

368
00:20:00.535 --> 00:20:03.538
You figured out if her husband's
Jason Bourne?

369
00:20:04.505 --> 00:20:08.142
Only his real passport
has been used for travel.

370
00:20:08.208 --> 00:20:10.845
Then why all the other
phony IDs?

371
00:20:11.846 --> 00:20:13.246
Finances.

372
00:20:14.048 --> 00:20:17.284
Account attached to one of them
shows money moving from Blake

373
00:20:17.350 --> 00:20:19.486
through shell corporations

374
00:20:19.554 --> 00:20:22.790
to Equatorial Guinea and back.

375
00:20:22.857 --> 00:20:25.526
Wait. Equatorial Guinea's
part of the Sahel.

376
00:20:25.593 --> 00:20:28.763
where the car bomb's
tradecraft points to.

377
00:20:36.269 --> 00:20:38.106
Well. maybe
he's masking the payment

378
00:20:38.172 --> 00:20:39.674
for a hit out on his wife.

379
00:20:39.741 --> 00:20:42.043
You think he is a suspect now?

380
00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:45.913
He was with her during
both assassination attempts.

381
00:20:45.980 --> 00:20:48.281
I mean. being in the line
of fire's a hell of an alibi.

382
00:20:48.348 --> 00:20:51.284
Okay. What's his motive?

383
00:20:51.351 --> 00:20:53.453
I mean. the marriage has
run its course.

384
00:20:53.521 --> 00:20:55.388
and he'd rather collect
life insurance

385
00:20:55.455 --> 00:20:58.025
than face a judge
in divorce court.

386
00:20:58.826 --> 00:21:01.428
I know a broken relationship
when I see one.

387
00:21:07.668 --> 00:21:09.436
Do you have anything to eat?

388
00:21:10.972 --> 00:21:13.641
Uh... Got some elk steaks.

389
00:21:14.441 --> 00:21:16.577
I spotted some Uncrustables
in the fridge

390
00:21:16.644 --> 00:21:18.813
for the non-cavemen.

391
00:21:32.359 --> 00:21:34.562
I'm having trouble
with cell service.

392
00:21:34.629 --> 00:21:36.764
Downside of living
in the 19th century.

393
00:21:37.565 --> 00:21:40.067
The. uh. porch might get you
a bar or two.

394
00:21:48.308 --> 00:21:51.012
How you holding up?

395
00:21:52.046 --> 00:21:55.583
Some psycho wanting my mom dead
is kind of messing with me.

396
00:21:57.484 --> 00:21:58.853
We get it.

397
00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:01.088
Both of our dads died
because of their job.

398
00:22:03.958 --> 00:22:05.059
That's so awful.

399
00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:08.663
I lost my dad
in the line of duty.

400
00:22:08.729 --> 00:22:10.965
and Kayce's dad was
the governor.

401
00:22:11.032 --> 00:22:12.800
They find their killers?

402
00:22:12.867 --> 00:22:16.336
Chance to find my dad's gets me
out of bed in the morning.

403
00:22:17.404 --> 00:22:19.006
People on social media
were obsessed

404
00:22:19.073 --> 00:22:20.775
with trying to solve
your dad's murder.

405
00:22:20.842 --> 00:22:22.210
Hmm.

406
00:22:23.144 --> 00:22:26.013
- I don't think about it much.
- Oh. come on.

407
00:22:26.080 --> 00:22:28.516
You go man on fire
for victims you've never met.

408
00:22:28.583 --> 00:22:30.350
You're telling me you don't have
a list of suspects?

409
00:22:31.152 --> 00:22:34.454
Heard something about...
private contractors.

410
00:22:34.522 --> 00:22:36.591
Is it wrong
that I want something

411
00:22:36.657 --> 00:22:38.993
bad to happen
to whoever's after my mom?

412
00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:41.829
There's a big difference
between craving vengeance

413
00:22:41.896 --> 00:22:43.064
and getting it.

414
00:22:43.998 --> 00:22:46.234
I think about getting it plenty.

415
00:22:46.300 --> 00:22:48.236
This was my dad's.

416
00:22:48.302 --> 00:22:51.072
I carry it on the off chance
I ever meet his killer.

417
00:22:51.138 --> 00:22:53.107
But mostly it just gives me
a sense of control

418
00:22:53.174 --> 00:22:55.643
over the thing that owns me.

419
00:23:03.684 --> 00:23:05.485
- Yeah?
<i>- Coyo.</i>

420
00:23:05.553 --> 00:23:07.755
husband's starting
to look shady.

421
00:23:07.822 --> 00:23:10.291
He's got aliases.
international payments.

422
00:23:10.358 --> 00:23:12.425
<i>I think he could be involved.</i>

423
00:23:12.492 --> 00:23:14.195
Well. there's a twist.

424
00:23:14.262 --> 00:23:16.697
<i>I'm gonna need you</i>
<i>to feel him out. okay?</i>

425
00:23:16.764 --> 00:23:17.798
Yeah.

426
00:23:25.039 --> 00:23:26.507
Blake?

427
00:23:31.913 --> 00:23:33.480
Blake?

428
00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:37.952
Blake?

429
00:23:42.223 --> 00:23:44.058
How could he be missing? He was
under your team's protection.

430
00:23:44.125 --> 00:23:46.127
My marshals think that
he left on his own.

431
00:23:46.193 --> 00:23:48.262
Fallon is his whole life.
He wouldn't.

432
00:23:48.329 --> 00:23:50.564
Well. we have security footage

433
00:23:50.631 --> 00:23:52.566
from your husband's
disappearance.

434
00:23:55.303 --> 00:23:58.039
Does the name Joseph Petit
mean anything to you?

435
00:23:59.073 --> 00:24:00.141
No.

436
00:24:00.207 --> 00:24:03.711
Joseph Petit is an alias
your husband uses.

437
00:24:03.778 --> 00:24:06.514
Alias? I don't follow.

438
00:24:06.580 --> 00:24:07.915
Your husband keeps
false passports

439
00:24:07.982 --> 00:24:09.884
in a wall in your home.
You aware of that?

440
00:24:12.787 --> 00:24:15.056
And is there anything else
he could be hiding?

441
00:24:15.122 --> 00:24:18.059
Are you investigating
my husband?

442
00:24:22.163 --> 00:24:23.664
Should we be?

443
00:24:26.600 --> 00:24:29.103
We pulled this
from surveillance cameras

444
00:24:29.170 --> 00:24:30.805
on our colleague's ranch.

445
00:24:33.641 --> 00:24:36.711
Seems like
he was expecting them.

446
00:24:44.484 --> 00:24:46.821
They kidnapped him?

447
00:24:46.887 --> 00:24:49.957
Has he been the target
all along?

448
00:24:50.758 --> 00:24:52.760
It's possible.

449
00:24:52.827 --> 00:24:54.095
But why?

450
00:24:54.161 --> 00:24:56.831
We were hoping you...
you might know. Your Honor.

451
00:24:56.897 --> 00:24:59.867
My husband of 25 years

452
00:24:59.934 --> 00:25:02.236
has been living
a secret life. so

453
00:25:02.303 --> 00:25:06.741
clearly. I don't know anything.

454
00:25:13.814 --> 00:25:15.716
We'll give you a moment.

455
00:25:24.792 --> 00:25:27.028
Well. that was brutal.

456
00:25:27.094 --> 00:25:29.163
Well. we had to tell her
the truth.

457
00:25:29.230 --> 00:25:30.698
I know.

458
00:25:30.765 --> 00:25:33.300
And we just unraveled
a marriage. and we still

459
00:25:33.367 --> 00:25:35.036
don't have answers.

460
00:25:35.102 --> 00:25:37.905
Maybe Blake's hard drive
will help.

461
00:25:37.972 --> 00:25:39.306
My man.

462
00:25:40.307 --> 00:25:42.143
Let me see.

463
00:25:44.445 --> 00:25:46.313
Fallon. you want some company?

464
00:25:46.380 --> 00:25:49.150
No. Just...
give me a minute.

465
00:25:53.454 --> 00:25:56.791
Poor kid. She's literally
worried sick about her dad.

466
00:25:56.857 --> 00:25:58.592
Given that Blake was
grabbed nearby.

467
00:25:58.659 --> 00:26:00.027
Cal wants us to clear out.

468
00:26:00.828 --> 00:26:02.797
All Fallon knows
is that her father's missing.

469
00:26:02.863 --> 00:26:04.298
That's all she needs to know.

470
00:26:10.471 --> 00:26:15.042
We found some information
we'd like to share with you.

471
00:26:15.109 --> 00:26:17.411
Your husband attended
the opening of a clinic

472
00:26:17.478 --> 00:26:20.581
in Equatorial Guinea
about six months ago. right?

473
00:26:20.648 --> 00:26:22.249
-Yes.
-That clinic

474
00:26:22.316 --> 00:26:24.151
was run by Luis Andeme.

475
00:26:24.218 --> 00:26:26.787
He's an activist
against the repressive regime

476
00:26:26.854 --> 00:26:28.355
of President Bindong.

477
00:26:28.422 --> 00:26:30.559
So this is payback for Blake
giving medical supplies

478
00:26:30.624 --> 00:26:32.561
to the resistance?

479
00:26:32.626 --> 00:26:34.095
That hard drive contains

480
00:26:34.161 --> 00:26:37.566
evidence showing Andeme
convinced Blake to use his

481
00:26:37.631 --> 00:26:40.267
nonprofit infrastructure to
smuggle weapons for his cause.

482
00:26:40.334 --> 00:26:42.303
What?

483
00:26:42.369 --> 00:26:46.607
You-You're telling me
Blake's an arms dealer?

484
00:26:46.674 --> 00:26:50.878
President Bindong's daughter
was killed last month. Car bomb.

485
00:26:50.945 --> 00:26:54.315
Made by the resistance
with explosives

486
00:26:54.381 --> 00:26:57.218
your husband supplied.

487
00:26:58.986 --> 00:27:01.523
And then. three days ago.
Blake received

488
00:27:01.590 --> 00:27:04.125
e-mails from Bindong's henchmen.
threatening death

489
00:27:04.191 --> 00:27:06.026
unless he turned over
information

490
00:27:06.093 --> 00:27:09.263
about everyone
he has shipped weapons to.

491
00:27:10.397 --> 00:27:13.434
Blake probably
overheard us discussing

492
00:27:13.501 --> 00:27:16.237
the construction of the car
bomb. and he connected the dots.

493
00:27:16.303 --> 00:27:17.671
contacted them to meet.

494
00:27:17.738 --> 00:27:20.741
Trying to protect
you and Fallon.

495
00:27:20.808 --> 00:27:23.711
And when they get

496
00:27:23.777 --> 00:27:26.013
what they need from him...

497
00:27:27.114 --> 00:27:29.683
Can't you identify
these monsters?

498
00:27:29.750 --> 00:27:32.353
FRS returns identities
that seem to be scrubbed

499
00:27:32.419 --> 00:27:33.854
in ways often seen with people

500
00:27:33.921 --> 00:27:35.823
who've done covert work
with the U.S. government.

501
00:27:38.125 --> 00:27:40.661
Their files can be unclassified

502
00:27:40.728 --> 00:27:43.764
with a warrant
signed by a federal judge.

503
00:27:45.232 --> 00:27:47.034
Shall we?

504
00:27:54.975 --> 00:27:57.211
Finding you a secure location.

505
00:27:58.078 --> 00:28:00.147
And my mom's worried
about a concert.

506
00:28:00.214 --> 00:28:01.650
On it. Cal.

507
00:28:01.715 --> 00:28:03.552
Guys in the red van
are Americans--

508
00:28:03.618 --> 00:28:05.319
Rylan Hightower and Nate Porter.

509
00:28:05.386 --> 00:28:07.288
Ex-Delta Force.
now private contractors.

510
00:28:07.354 --> 00:28:10.724
They both did FID
for Bindong's forces in 2022.

511
00:28:11.492 --> 00:28:13.227
Is their contracting group
out of Texas?

512
00:28:13.294 --> 00:28:16.096
Unknown. but Hightower has
property near Clyde Park.

513
00:28:16.163 --> 00:28:18.098
That might be
where they're headed.

514
00:28:18.165 --> 00:28:20.201
That's only
a few miles from here.

515
00:28:24.939 --> 00:28:27.741
What do we do about...

516
00:28:28.577 --> 00:28:30.844
Blake doesn't have much time.

517
00:28:59.507 --> 00:29:02.743
-This is where my dad is?
-We're about to find out.

518
00:29:02.810 --> 00:29:05.012
I can't handle this.
I'm freaking out.

519
00:29:05.813 --> 00:29:08.916
Fallon. it's gonna be okay.

520
00:29:09.817 --> 00:29:12.786
DOJ wants to talk to these guys
about their work with Bindong.

521
00:29:12.853 --> 00:29:15.022
so we need them alive.

522
00:29:15.089 --> 00:29:16.924
Blake doesn't have time.

523
00:29:16.991 --> 00:29:18.926
I'm going in now.
You stay with Fallon.

524
00:29:18.993 --> 00:29:20.327
One is none. remember?

525
00:29:20.394 --> 00:29:22.129
Especially against
special forces operators.

526
00:29:22.196 --> 00:29:24.098
Cal and Belle are
ten minutes out.

527
00:29:26.267 --> 00:29:28.002
You ever wish that help
would've gotten to your dad

528
00:29:28.068 --> 00:29:29.470
ten minutes faster?

529
00:29:51.025 --> 00:29:54.995
Give us some names
or fry some more.

530
00:29:56.030 --> 00:29:57.164
Please. I told you.

531
00:29:57.231 --> 00:29:59.800
I don't know. I don't know.

532
00:29:59.867 --> 00:30:00.901
Let's help him remember. yeah?

533
00:30:00.968 --> 00:30:03.003
U.S. Marshals!

534
00:30:10.077 --> 00:30:12.413
You okay?

535
00:30:12.479 --> 00:30:15.449
I will be
when you get the other guy.

536
00:31:13.842 --> 00:31:15.577
It's just here.

537
00:31:21.649 --> 00:31:23.150
Oh. thank God.

538
00:31:37.297 --> 00:31:39.734
You haven't said a word
to your dad.

539
00:31:39.801 --> 00:31:41.435
What do I say?

540
00:31:41.503 --> 00:31:44.171
Thanks for nearly getting Mom
shot and blown up?

541
00:31:44.238 --> 00:31:46.273
I'd just be grateful
they're alive.

542
00:31:46.340 --> 00:31:47.809
I am.

543
00:31:47.876 --> 00:31:49.276
But...

544
00:31:50.077 --> 00:31:52.079
...is my dad a monster?

545
00:31:54.582 --> 00:31:58.620
I once took down this fugitive
my dad had put away.

546
00:31:59.453 --> 00:32:01.656
The guy swore
my old man was corrupt.

547
00:32:01.723 --> 00:32:03.725
It shook me up.

548
00:32:03.792 --> 00:32:05.627
Do you think he was dirty?

549
00:32:05.693 --> 00:32:08.395
I think that I would
love the chance to ask him.

550
00:32:09.764 --> 00:32:11.331
No father's perfect.

551
00:32:12.266 --> 00:32:13.735
And once you realize he was just
trying to protect you

552
00:32:13.802 --> 00:32:16.838
in his own messed-up way.
your anger will fade.

553
00:32:17.906 --> 00:32:20.374
I just hope that. if you ever
do decide to forgive him.

554
00:32:20.441 --> 00:32:23.110
he's still around to hear it.

555
00:32:47.401 --> 00:32:48.335
Hey.

556
00:32:48.402 --> 00:32:49.470
Hey.

557
00:32:49.537 --> 00:32:51.205
I just closed the Ayers file.

558
00:32:51.271 --> 00:32:54.776
Should we go join the others
at the Bullet?

559
00:32:54.843 --> 00:32:56.578
Pass.

560
00:32:56.644 --> 00:32:59.246
Come on.

561
00:32:59.313 --> 00:33:01.181
Is Maddie still
freezing you out?

562
00:33:01.248 --> 00:33:03.050
You know. one of us
can order for you.

563
00:33:03.116 --> 00:33:07.421
avoid any further
awkward interactions.

564
00:33:08.723 --> 00:33:11.391
Look. go have fun
with your teammates.

565
00:33:13.093 --> 00:33:15.128
Well. this is a pickle.

566
00:33:15.964 --> 00:33:18.733
See. I really need
that buffer zone

567
00:33:18.800 --> 00:33:21.636
between work and home
that you suggested.

568
00:33:21.703 --> 00:33:24.271
but I can't leave you here
like this.

569
00:33:26.674 --> 00:33:29.978
Bourbon?
That's an aggressive choice.

570
00:33:30.879 --> 00:33:35.082
Man. we just told the judge
half her life is a lie.

571
00:33:35.148 --> 00:33:37.417
Move.

572
00:33:37.484 --> 00:33:39.621
I mean. if that doesn't call
for hard stuff...

573
00:33:42.289 --> 00:33:43.992
...I don't know what does.

574
00:33:57.104 --> 00:33:59.007
<i>Dedicate your life</i>
<i>to someone. only to find out</i>

575
00:33:59.072 --> 00:34:00.508
you barely know 'em.

576
00:34:00.575 --> 00:34:03.076
A family like that
is the reason why

577
00:34:03.143 --> 00:34:04.812
I remain eternally single.

578
00:34:04.879 --> 00:34:06.179
Bulldogger's loss.

579
00:34:06.246 --> 00:34:07.649
What's next for you?

580
00:34:07.715 --> 00:34:09.116
Bull rider? Rodeo clown?

581
00:34:09.182 --> 00:34:13.287
No. What about you? When are you
asking out this mystery girl?

582
00:34:13.353 --> 00:34:15.990
Probably too complicated
for it to ever work out.

583
00:34:16.056 --> 00:34:17.825
That's how you know it's right.

584
00:34:17.892 --> 00:34:21.161
I don't have a lot of experience
dating non-Native women.

585
00:34:21.228 --> 00:34:22.462
Just be confident.

586
00:34:22.530 --> 00:34:24.032
Not exactly my strong suit.

587
00:34:24.097 --> 00:34:27.501
Any advice on asking out
women around here from a local?

588
00:34:27.569 --> 00:34:29.236
Well. the last time
I asked out anyone.

589
00:34:29.303 --> 00:34:31.104
I was in high school
and she was from Broken Rock.

590
00:34:31.940 --> 00:34:33.575
If I'm gonna crash and burn.

591
00:34:33.641 --> 00:34:36.578
might as well have my teammates
here to put out the flames.

592
00:34:39.013 --> 00:34:40.247
She's here?

593
00:34:40.314 --> 00:34:42.149
Here goes nothing.

594
00:34:53.493 --> 00:34:55.063
You guys need refills?

595
00:34:55.128 --> 00:34:56.731
Um. sure.

596
00:34:58.800 --> 00:35:00.635
Also. uh...

597
00:35:00.702 --> 00:35:02.637
I was wondering.

598
00:35:02.704 --> 00:35:04.872
would you maybe like to go
on a date sometime?

599
00:35:06.007 --> 00:35:06.941
With you?

600
00:35:07.008 --> 00:35:08.543
Maybe.

601
00:35:08.610 --> 00:35:09.978
I mean...

602
00:35:10.044 --> 00:35:12.013
yeah. with me.

603
00:35:12.080 --> 00:35:14.414
Yeah. I-I'd love to.

604
00:35:14.481 --> 00:35:16.684
I was hoping
you might be interested.

605
00:35:16.751 --> 00:35:20.888
I just thought maybe
you'd chicken out.

606
00:35:20.955 --> 00:35:23.524
No way. I'm a confident guy.

607
00:35:23.591 --> 00:35:27.260
Well. you must be.
asking out your boss's daughter.

608
00:35:29.564 --> 00:35:32.667
Maddie was maybe three.

609
00:35:32.734 --> 00:35:34.401
and we went to. we went

610
00:35:34.468 --> 00:35:37.972
to the San Diego Zoo.
She lost her mind.

611
00:35:39.674 --> 00:35:43.678
And I was. I was tucking her in
that night. and...

612
00:35:43.745 --> 00:35:46.547
she said.
"This is the best day ever."

613
00:35:52.386 --> 00:35:54.856
Well. you know.
no one's childhood

614
00:35:54.922 --> 00:35:56.791
stays frozen in time.

615
00:35:56.858 --> 00:35:59.292
Look at Fallon.
She just found out her father's

616
00:35:59.359 --> 00:36:01.929
the villain
in someone else's story.

617
00:36:01.996 --> 00:36:03.898
What about Pauline?

618
00:36:04.666 --> 00:36:07.535
I mean. Blake wasn't
who she thought he was. either.

619
00:36:07.602 --> 00:36:10.838
-Mm.
-I mean. does their...

620
00:36:10.905 --> 00:36:12.272
does their marriage survive?

621
00:36:15.375 --> 00:36:18.178
You know how tough marriage is.

622
00:36:21.716 --> 00:36:23.818
Would your marriage survive
if your...

623
00:36:23.885 --> 00:36:25.653
husband was living
a secret life?

624
00:36:25.720 --> 00:36:28.388
There's nothing
I don't know about Jared.

625
00:36:28.455 --> 00:36:29.824
- Really?
- Really.

626
00:36:29.891 --> 00:36:33.226
Given everything
that you shield from him?

627
00:36:34.095 --> 00:36:35.863
You really think
a cop can't tell

628
00:36:35.930 --> 00:36:37.497
you're sitting on something?

629
00:36:37.565 --> 00:36:39.499
Come on. Out with it.

630
00:36:39.567 --> 00:36:43.137
You have been weird all day.
Give it to me.

631
00:36:43.203 --> 00:36:45.873
Look. it's not my place.

632
00:36:45.940 --> 00:36:47.942
but I-I know that you would do
the same for me

633
00:36:48.009 --> 00:36:50.078
if the situations
were reversed. so...

634
00:36:56.751 --> 00:36:59.386
What situation?

635
00:37:04.025 --> 00:37:06.460
I saw Jared with another woman.

636
00:37:18.773 --> 00:37:21.676
He's supposed to be discreet.

637
00:37:22.577 --> 00:37:25.847
What? Wait. that's it?

638
00:37:25.913 --> 00:37:28.750
Okay.

639
00:37:28.816 --> 00:37:32.687
Not that I have
to justify anything.

640
00:37:32.754 --> 00:37:34.522
but...

641
00:37:35.623 --> 00:37:38.192
...people change.

642
00:37:38.258 --> 00:37:40.293
You know. years go by.

643
00:37:40.360 --> 00:37:43.430
My work undercover
kept us apart.

644
00:37:44.565 --> 00:37:49.369
Things slipped... away.

645
00:37:50.470 --> 00:37:52.607
Why... why stay together?

646
00:37:52.673 --> 00:37:55.375
Keeping my family whole
for Braxton

647
00:37:55.442 --> 00:37:59.312
is my priority.

648
00:38:00.815 --> 00:38:03.383
Seems kind of lonely.
though. no?

649
00:38:24.772 --> 00:38:26.607
That was a terrible idea.

650
00:38:26.674 --> 00:38:30.845
Yeah. Sorry. uh.
the-the booze and long day.

651
00:38:30.912 --> 00:38:33.748
Yeah. Uh...

652
00:38:35.116 --> 00:38:36.416
Let's just call it a night.

653
00:38:58.338 --> 00:38:59.540
Guy who doesn't drink

654
00:38:59.607 --> 00:39:01.042
pining for the bartender.
Go figure.

655
00:39:05.646 --> 00:39:07.949
You really haven't
asked anyone out since Monica?

656
00:39:12.286 --> 00:39:13.688
Did your mom date
after your dad?

657
00:39:15.223 --> 00:39:17.457
Oh. now we're getting somewhere.

658
00:39:17.525 --> 00:39:19.026
Does this have
anything to do

659
00:39:19.093 --> 00:39:21.128
with the Weaver Ranch swag
at your house?

660
00:39:21.195 --> 00:39:22.964
Hey. Dolly ambushed me.

661
00:39:23.030 --> 00:39:24.165
Really?

662
00:39:24.232 --> 00:39:26.033
Drive-by date?

663
00:39:26.100 --> 00:39:28.236
Oh. I underestimated this chick.

664
00:39:29.971 --> 00:39:32.640
Did you enjoy it?

665
00:39:32.707 --> 00:39:36.476
As much as you and I focus
on avenging our dead...

666
00:39:36.544 --> 00:39:38.512
guess we can betray them. too.

667
00:39:39.313 --> 00:39:42.482
Hanging out with Dolly
felt like cheating on Monica.

668
00:39:43.450 --> 00:39:44.518
I see.

669
00:39:47.021 --> 00:39:48.421
Yeah. my mom dated.

670
00:39:48.488 --> 00:39:50.057
Then she met a great guy.

671
00:39:50.124 --> 00:39:51.692
and I realized

672
00:39:51.759 --> 00:39:54.562
that she wasn't replacing my dad
in her heart.

673
00:39:54.629 --> 00:39:57.798
she was just making room
for someone new.

674
00:40:00.201 --> 00:40:01.401
What about your dad?

675
00:40:03.771 --> 00:40:05.806
Uh. nothing serious.

676
00:40:05.873 --> 00:40:09.076
He didn't have room
for anyone or anything else

677
00:40:09.143 --> 00:40:11.478
other than anger
at losing my mom.

678
00:40:12.479 --> 00:40:14.815
And do you think Monica
would want that for you?

679
00:40:17.450 --> 00:40:18.786
I'd love the chance to ask her.

680
00:41:10.470 --> 00:41:12.773
You gonna get back
on that horse?

681
00:41:14.141 --> 00:41:16.110
Not sure I'm ready.

682
00:41:17.411 --> 00:41:19.613
I'm sorry about the other night.
I think I overstepped.

683
00:41:19.680 --> 00:41:21.716
Call it a family trait.

684
00:41:24.518 --> 00:41:27.154
Is another tour
out of the question?

685
00:41:28.422 --> 00:41:31.225
It's just a horseback ride.

685
00:41:32.305 --> 00:42:32.660
